---
import Base from "@layouts/Base.astro";
import { brand } from "../brand/config";
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="How the Society handles your data." canonicalPath="/privacy/">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p>
        The {brand.shortName} remembers what you choose to share, and nothing more. Member memory is transparent,
        editable and removable. The {brand.shortName} does not silently enrich members from public sources.
      </p>

      <h2>What we keep</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your email address (to write to you)</li>
        <li>Your first name and any preferred name you give us</li>
        <li>Your chapter or metro area, if you give it (so chapter letters are accurate)</li>
        <li>Your birthday, if you give it (so a card can be sent on the right day)</li>
        <li>Your postal address, if you opt in to physical mail (so we can post to you)</li>
        <li>Any other facts you choose to share, plus your do-not-mention list</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we do not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We do not enrich your record from public sources without asking.</li>
        <li>
          We do not sell your data. We do not share it with third parties except as required to
          deliver the service (Resend for email, Cloudflare for hosting, Stripe for billing when
          billing is enabled).
        </li>
        <li>We do not use your data to train general AI models.</li>
        <li>We do not infer sensitive personal categories for personalisation.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your controls</h2>
      <p>
        When the member portal is available, you will be able to see exactly what the
        {brand.shortName} remembers about you, edit or remove any fact, mark any fact as "do not mention",
        and export a copy of your data. Until the portal is available, you can ask the operator to do
        this on your behalf.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention</h2>
      <p>
        When you ask to be forgotten, the {brand.shortName} stops future personalisation and removes your
        personal data subject to legitimate retention requirements (for example, financial records we
        are required to keep for a number of years).
      </p>

      <h2>Full policy</h2>
      <p>
        The full privacy policy will be published before the paid launch. The summary above is not
        the policy; it is the plain-language preview.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
